encoding  utf-8
survey WallStreet -title "Wall Street"

#Surveyed 7/7/7
#Team Julie H, Bill C, Mike R, Pete B
#MCG Standard Compass + Clino
#Tape Measureements adjusted for 20ms of missing tape
#First survey station is the permanently marked S22 in the main stream
#Stations ws1 to ws10 are along the passage from the stream (no name ? Threadneedle Street (Mike R, Bill C)).
#Stations wp1-wp12 are in Wall Street.
#A survey mark (triangle) was scratched on a raised rock at ws8 this is at the junction with Wall Street
#At WS9 there are some large fallen blocks, the largest approx 2x3x3m.
#The passage that leaves the stream at SS2 closes down with small choked and calcited blocks 2m? beyond ws11.
#On the left between ws10 and ws11 there are some high avens.
#A small stream flows from ws1 to the main stream.
#Wp1 is at the top of the Wall Street break through mound.
#Wp4 was on the arched roof, L+R are the width of the passage on the floor.
#Some of the later 0 elevations were taken be using stations on a horizontal crystal tideline.
#Wp6 was ontop of a stal column, L+R are the width of the passage on the floor.
#Wp11 is a dead end, two legs from wp10.
#
#LRUD at station n is taken with the view from station n-1 to station n
#
#Station1, Station2, Distance (m), Compass Bearing degrees, Elevation degrees, Left (m), Right(m), Up(m), Down(m)
#
#Distances with ? are unmeasured estimates.
#In Wall Street itself the compass and clino were getting very difficult to
#read (wet and muddy). Bring on some better technology!
#
#I was scribe and tape, Julie then Mike and Pete were Compass + Clino. Pete
#did some tape work too. I have some profile sketches in the notebook. If you
#want them, I could scan them for you.

  centreline

    units clino compass degree
    units length meter
    team "Bill Chadwick" notes
    team "Julie Hesketh" 
    team "Mike Richardson"
    team "Peat Bennett"
    instrument length  "MCG tape (missing end)"
    instrument compass  "MCG"  
    instrument clino  "MCG"
    date 2007.07.07

    #declination -3.001 deg  	# BGS at 2007.07.07 (2007.52) 51.2987N 2.71038W
    #declination -3.002 deg  	# BGS at 2007.07.07 (2007.52) 51.2987N 2.71038W Alt 0.2km.  2010 Model.  Updated Nov 2011
				# http://www.geomag.bgs.ac.uk/gifs/wmm_calc.html
    declination -2.449 deg    	# Allign to grid, Grid North +0.5535 deg

    extend left
    data normal from to length compass clino left right up down
    s22	ws1	4.97	226	+30	1.80	1.70	3.5	0.00 # Up estimated
    ws1	ws2	4.50	290	+26	1.25	0.50	2.30	0.10
    ws2	ws3	11.50	278	0	0.60	1.64	0.70	0.10
    ws3	ws4	4.11	264	+8	0.24	0.23	3.5	0.60 # Up estimated
    ws4	ws5	3.27	284	+4	0.67	0.75	0.30	0.32
    ws5	ws6	3.56	278	+20	0.94	1.00	1.70	0.70
    ws6	ws7	7.94	270	+22	1.12	1.35	1.63	0.90
    ws7	ws8	5.36	287	+12	0.90	1.30	8.5	0.63 # Up estimated
	mark ws8 fixed
	station ws8 "WS8 A survey mark (triangle) was scratched on a raised rock" continuation attr code "fixed" attr Name "WS8"
    ws8	ws9	9.47	278	+23	0.50	0.90	10.0	0.10 # Up estimated
    ws9	ws10	4.54	290	+12	1.50	1.20	1.10	0.60
    ws10 ws11	5.40	279	+5	0.65	0.57	0.50	0.55

    extend right    
    ws8	wp1	4.25	164	+20	0.86	0.44	4.0	0.00 # Up estimated
    wp1	wp2	4.82	145	+10	0.13	0.13	0.79	0.00
    wp2	wp3	2.13	139	-3	0.51	0.74	0.51	0.51
    wp3	wp4	7.61	128	+8	1.25	1.25	0.0	0.94
    wp4	wp5	5.51	122	-5	0.00	1.09	0.84	0.49
    wp5	wp6	5.35	148	0	0.13	0.13	0.48	0.55
    wp6	wp7	3.15	120	0	0.00	1.44	2.0	1.15 # Up estimated
    wp7	wp8	1.58	228	0	0.54	0.00	1.60	1.11
    wp8	wp9	3.22	166	0	0.44	0.00	0.87	0.00
    wp9	wp10	2.32	140	-7	0.00	0.92	1.18	1.20
    data normal from to length compass clino
    wp10 wp11	4.0	105	0					# tape estimated
    wp10 wp12	10.0	260	0					# tape estimated
  endcentreline
endsurvey

 
